According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Graphite Felt Electrode Market was valued at USD 450 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 1.173 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 14.8% during the forecast period. Graphite felt electrodes are porous, high-surface-area carbon materials manufactured from PAN or rayon precursor fibers and are widely used in flow batteries, fuel cells, electrochemical reactors and other high-performance applications.
