Why Is Demand Increasing?
Expansion of electric-arc furnaces: Steel manufacturers are upgrading production systems to improve efficiency and reduce carbon intensity.
Growth in energy storage: Vanadium redox flow batteries require high-surface-area electrodes for grid-scale energy storage.
Recycled-metal production: Growing metal recycling activity is increasing demand for efficient high-temperature electrode materials.
Advanced electrode technologies: Surface activation and catalyst coating improve electrode performance.
Specialty alloy production: High-purity graphite felt is gaining opportunities in aerospace and advanced-material applications.
Advanced Electrode Technology Watch
The Graphite Felt Electrode Market is benefiting from simultaneous growth in steelmaking modernization and energy-storage applications. Flow-battery installations represented approximately 30% of sales in the base year, while high-purity PAN-based felt for aerospace alloys is identified as an emerging high-growth opportunity.
Thermal and chemical surface activation technologies are increasingly important because they can improve pore accessibility, electrolyte wettability and electrochemical performance. Manufacturers are also investing in customized electrode geometries and surface treatments to meet application-specific requirements.
